+        // [ff9mapkit s89] THE FIELD'S OBJECTS -- every other actor on the field, and what the engine's own
+        // player-vs-object collision does with it. Before this the player was the only object published, so
+        // the driver's router found NPCs by walking into them, and could not tell a villager it may push
+        // through from one that holds the player forever -- on a tight map, a true movement lock.
+        //
+        // THE SET is what WalkMesh.Collision walks for the player (mode 0): the active object list, actors
+        // only (cid 4; regions and code entries never collide), minus the player. An actor with no model,
+        // or hidden, still collides if its collision bit says so -- an invisible wall -- so it is listed
+        // with `shown` false, never dropped.
+        //   r      4*(obj.collRad + player.collRad): the centre distance inside which the engine calls it a
+        //          collision (disdif < -1: a hit must beat 0 by more than 1). collRad is SetObjectLogicalSize's
+        //          2nd argument (PosObj default 16). The pair only collides while |dy| < 400 -- the driver
+        //          compares `y` to the player's.
+        //   coll   the pair is skipped only when the PLAYER has flag 4 AND the object has flag 2 (actors are
+        //          born with 4, so in practice: object flag 2 = walk-through). A field debug mode skips all.
+        //   solid  coll and object flag 16: touching it resets sLockTimer, so CheckCollFallback never
+        //          reaches 25 and never opens its walk-through window. Without 16 the push-out is released
+        //          after ~26 unbroken colliding MovePC calls. Field 2207 at SC 9840 skips the fallback, so
+        //          there every collidable object is solid -- unless the window was already open on entry
+        //          (sLockTimer < 0 is then frozen until a flag-16 contact zeroes it; see `pushout`).
+        //   range  the entry HAS a tag-2 (Range) function. range_r = r + speed + 60 is where the engine's
+        //          per-tick search (CollisionRequest, mode 2) REQUESTS it: with the player under control,
+        //          standing still or not -- a contact script (a warp, a battle) the router must not blunder
+        //          into. null when coll is false (mode 2 uses the same pair rule). Only the closest such entry
+        //          is requested per tick, and only while it is idle (Request needs level > 1); CheckNPCPush
+        //          exempts fields 103/107 sid 3-4 and 1856 sid 5-6, which this does not mirror.
+        //   talk   the entry HAS a tag-3 (talk) function. talk_r = 4*(obj.talkRad + player.talkRad) + speed
+        //          + 60 is the talk search (mode 4), null when object flag 8 bars talk. When that search
+        //          shows the talk icon it requests the TALK object's tag 2 instead of running mode 2, so an
+        //          entry with range AND talk may also fire its Range inside talk_r while the player faces it.
+        //          (Both searches also box |dx|,|dz| < 2048, which only a radius above 2048 can feel.)
+        //   shown  the renderer gate: a GameObject, flag 1, frontCamera (projected depth in range) and at
+        //          least one mesh not hidden by HideMesh (a model with no mesh list counts as shown). null
+        //          when the GameObject carries no HonoBehavior: the gate never drives its renderers.
+        //   moving a scripted walk in progress (actMove), a controller path, or displaced this tick (the
+        //          engine's own walk-animation test). A walker held by a collision still reads true.
+        // r/coll/solid/range_r/talk_r are relations to the player; with no controlled player they are null.
+        // `pushout` is the push-out's GLOBAL state, which decides whether a non-solid body blocks RIGHT NOW:
+        // slock = EventEngine.sLockTimer (< 0: the walk-through window is open and every non-16 object is
+        // passable), scoll = SCollTimer, slockfree = sLockFree (set by the CLOSEST colliding object), and
+        // fallback = whether CheckCollFallback runs here at all. Off a field both values are null, and ANY
+        // failure makes both null: a partial list would tell a router that a blocked path is clear.
+        // Additive -- the protocol `v` stays 5.
